This is a known change in .NET 10. Android now defaults to **edge-to-edge** mode, and `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` no longer drives layout changes. The replacement is to react to **window insets** so your layout automatically adjusts for the keyboard (IME).

## Solution

**1. Ensure edge-to-edge is active (default in .NET 10):**

In `MainActivity.cs` or your `MauiProgram.cs`, edge-to-edge is on by default. Don't disable it.

**2. Use padding that responds to keyboard insets:**

In your page or layout, set the `android:fitsSystemWindows` equivalent by applying an IME-aware bottom padding. In .NET MAUI / .NET 10, use the new `SafeAreaRegions` or handle it in the platform code:

```xml
<!-- In your XAML page -->
<Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" ... />
    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1" x:Name="InputBar">
        <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand" />
        <Button Text="Send" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
</Grid>
```

**3. Apply keyboard inset handling on Android (`Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`):**

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        // React to IME (keyboard) insets
        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetsListener());
    }

    private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

            // Use the larger of IME or nav bar bottom inset
            int bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom);
            v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottom);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

**Key points:**

| .NET 9 approach | .NET 10 replacement |
|---|---|
| `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` | Window insets via `ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener` |
| `adjustResize` in manifest | Edge-to-edge + IME insets (default) |

This makes your input bar slide up exactly by the keyboard height. The `CollectionView` shrinks accordingly, keeping your chat messages visible above the input.
